{"id":"dualsense-edge-composite","name":"DualSense Edge (PS5) (composite USB)","vendor":"Sony","vid":"0x054C","pid":"0x0DF2","productString":"DualSense Edge Wireless Controller","manufacturerString":"Sony Interactive Entertainment","type":"gamepad","connection":"usb","descriptor":"","inputReportSize":64,"inputDefaults":[{"byte":49,"value":128},{"byte":50,"value":0},{"byte":51,"value":0},{"byte":52,"value":0}],"notes":"Issue #39 follow-up: the four-interface USB composite a real DualSense Edge presents, authored from a physical Edge's full lsusb -v probe (linux-hardware.org probe EAB445BFA5, Steam Deck host; mirrored in github.com/linuxhw/LsUSB). Configuration wTotalLength 227, bNumInterfaces 4, self-powered, 500 mA, high speed. The audio topology is byte-identical to the base DualSense (4-ch 48 kHz OUT with speaker channels 1/2 and voice-coil haptics 3/4, wChannelConfig 0x0033; 2-ch 48 kHz headset microphone IN). Two dump-confirmed differences from the base pad: HID wDescriptorLength 389 (matches this profile's Edge descriptor exactly) and HID interrupt IN bInterval 4 (1 ms input polling, the Edge's 1000 Hz USB input; OUT stays 6). Interface 3 is byte-identical to 'dualsense-edge', so the Edge feature reports 0x60-0x7B and codec carry over unchanged. Residuals, named precisely: no full-speed other-speed capture exists for the Edge, so GET_DESCRIPTOR(Other_Speed) stalls while the dump-confirmed Device Qualifier is served; and audioControls carries the BASE DualSense's captured wire ranges (identical advertised controls, same audio hardware per the topology) pending an Edge control-transfer capture. Uses the USB/IP create path (backend: usbip). The transport ships inside HIDMaestro.Core.dll and deploys itself on first use, so this profile needs nothing installed by hand. 'dualsense-edge' remains the UMDF2 single-interface profile and is unaffected.","buttonMap":[1,2,0,3,4,5,8,9,10,11,12,13],"triggerButtons":[6,7],"axisMap":{"0x32":"rightStickX","0x35":"rightStickY","0